// A single-line `if` condition may still use binary operators. The
// condition fix stops a condition at end of line, so an operator that belongs
// to the condition (on the same line) must still parse as part of it, not leak
// into the next option when inside a choice.

state
  score: 4
  bonus: 3

beat Start
  choice
    Open gate if score + bonus >= 5
      You opened the gate.
    Secret path if score + bonus >= 10
      A hidden route.
    Fallback if score > bonus
      The fallback.

/*
<test>
- choices: [0]
  expected: |
    + Open gate
    - Secret path
    + Fallback

    ~ You opened the gate.
</test>
*/
